/**
\page org_mitk_views_tensorreconstruction Tensor Reconstruction

The tensor view reconstructs diffusion tensors from a diffusion-weighted image (DWI). Select the DWI as "Diffusion-weighted Image", choose the method under "Advanced Settings" and press "Start Reconstruction":
\li <b>ITK Linear Least Squares:</b> a linear least-squares fit of the log-signal. Every volume is fitted with its own b-value, so DWIs with several shells are fitted correctly. "Ignore voxels with negative eigenvalues" leaves voxels whose tensor has a negative eigenvalue empty.
\li <b>With correction for negative eigenvalues:</b> the fit is repeated after smoothing the signal of voxels whose tensor has a negative eigenvalue; voxels that still have one are left empty.

Volumes whose b-value rounds to 0 are the baseline volumes; their mean is the non-diffusion weighted signal of a voxel. Voxels whose mean baseline signal is below the "B0 Threshold" are not reconstructed; while the threshold is changed, the excluded voxels are shown as an overlay on the DWI.

The reconstruction runs in the background: the application stays usable, and the buttons of the view are disabled until the result appears as a new node below the DWI (depending on the image size and method, after a few seconds to minutes). The same holds for the images generated from tensors below.

\imageMacro{tensor4.png,"Tensor image after reconstruction",16.00}

The view also generates images from a tensor image:
\li <b>ODF Image from Tensors:</b> the ODFs are initialized directly from the tensor values and normalized.
\li <b>Diffusion-weighted Image from Tensors:</b> a DWI with the chosen b-value and number of gradient directions (the directions are subdivisions of an icosahedron) and one baseline volume. The baseline signal is the l2-norm of the tensor; the diffusion-weighted volumes follow the tensor model.

*/
